\title{Congruences for the Integrality of $\dfrac{36n^3 - 19}{m}$}
\author{Jamal Agbanwa}
\date{\today}

\begin{document}

\begin{abstract}
We characterise all pairs $(m, n) \in \Z^2$ for which $m \mid 36n^3 - 19$,
equivalently $\frac{36n^3-19}{m}\in\Z$.
The condition reduces prime-by-prime to the solvability of
$36n^3 \equiv 19\pmod{p}$ for each prime $p\mid m$, which is a cubic-residue
problem governed by the splitting of $p$ modulo~$3$.
Using the Chinese Remainder Theorem we construct an explicit, unbounded
family of congruence pairs of increasing modulus.
The largest pair produced here has a $107$-digit modulus.
\end{abstract}

