\section{Explicit Congruence Pairs}
%------------------------------------------------------------------

\subsection{Small cases}

The two simplest solutions, which motivated this investigation, are:
\begin{align}
  n &\equiv 4 \pmod{5}, \label{eq:mod5}\\
  n &\equiv 10 \pmod{11}. \label{eq:mod11}
\end{align}
Both are verified directly: $36\cdot 4^3 - 19 = 2285 = 5\cdot 457$
and $36\cdot 10^3 - 19 = 35981 = 11\cdot 3271$.

\subsection{The 14-prime congruence}

Using the 14 primes $\mathcal{P}_{14} = \{5,11,17,19,23,29,41,47,53,59,71,83,89,101\}$
